{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The elders of Moab.</b> Sages." "<b>And divinations in their hand.</b> Rabbi Samuel the Nagid of Spain, of blessed memory, said its meaning is: \"and the likeness of divinations.\" I have seen [those who explain] \"in their hand,\" but he said nothing [beyond this]; rather it is as its plain sense. And Scripture informs that they sent to a diviner of divinations like him, and furthermore that he would not be able to delay, saying, \"I will not find a chosen day and a chosen hour to go and divine,\" for they are men of his craft. And the proof that its meaning is as it is [understood] is that Scripture said: \"the divination was in their hand\" [lit.]."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:57.532227835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}